# The session carries the `simpleRepl(...)` call site's surrounding
# source (with the call replaced by the marker), just like the `eval(gen)` form —
# so the embedded REPL body can introspect where it is embedded.
>>> {"op":"eval","code":"val src = simpleRepl[String] { s => s.complete(s.enclosingSource) }"}
~ "ok":true.*__evalBodyPlaceholder__

# The user's case: an simpleRepl nested in a `.map` sees the enclosing `.map(...)`.
>>> {"op":"eval","code":"val srcs = List(1, 2, 3).map(x => simpleRepl[Boolean](s => s.complete(s.enclosingSource.contains(\"map\"))))"}
~ "ok":true.*List\(true, true, true\)

# Call-site locals in scope at the simpleRepl call are captured into s.bindings;
# here each iteration captures `x`, so every embedded REPL session sees exactly one binding.
>>> {"op":"eval","code":"val ns = List(1, 2, 3).map(x => simpleRepl[Int](s => s.complete(s.bindings.length)))"}
~ "ok":true.*List\(1, 1, 1\)
